{
  "_note": "Sign-based inn/tavern name vocabulary. Names are built from a charge (the painted device on the sign) plus optional color, number, posture, pairing, or body-part, following the structural syntax of medieval and Renaissance English tavern signs. Consumed by src/innname.js. See docs/DESIGN.md 'Inn names' for the model, tuning, and how to add charges. Every charge lists concrete biomes (this project's five) and the tiers it can appear at; keep each biome stocked with charges that reach 'noble' so high-tier pools stay varied and biome-flavored rather than collapsing onto a handful of universal devices. A 'sign' is a bare, color-neutral noun phrase (no leading article): innname.js adds the article and injects the chosen color, so do not bake a tincture into a charge that has color:true.",

